Feyrock is a green stone that is not native to [[Færrin]] or to Færrin Prime. It comes from somewhere starward, toward the [[Godhome]] and the angelic, though nobody has ever located the source. Pieces turn up now and then and sell for large sums at auction, valued because they are rare and pretty. The street name comes from the belief that it is Fey in origin.

No magic anyone has been able to find lives in the stone, but a Feyrock carved as a leaf, found under [[Lyric Burke]]'s pillow, pulled toward the [[Verdant Expanse]]. In hand it vibrated as the forest neared; worn on its cord it lifted an inch above the wearer's chest and pointed the way deeper in, to the glade of a [[Bestiary/Fey|court of fey]] in the permanent dark. The pull stopped when the fey were killed.

The stone is a trader's stone. It is sold to the wealthy, and so only people with capital to spare ever handle it; a single stone is offered at forty-five thousand gold pieces. A jeweler tells a real one by its shine, which it holds without ever being polished, and by other signs that cannot be faked.

Rumours in [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/index|Hallia]] held that someone had worked out a blood ritual to make more Feyrock. The rumour was dismissed because more of the stone never appeared on the market. Whatever the truth of it, Feyrock grows through living flesh. In the [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Gullet/index|Gullet]] a man's leg had turned to the stone, and after he was dead it kept growing upward an inch or two a day and did not bleed when it was cut. A cut sliver of the stone is drawn to a particular page of the [[Phenomena/Gloaming Codex|Gloaming Codex]], and pressed there it pulls a person into the book.
